{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnTWBHjKRWu1K14dfPDC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking the independent τ result: the L16/17 head copy sums to 24.2 against a null of about −0.4 ± 4.8, roughly 5σ, with all eight heads positive. L12–15 look mixed, though L15 heads 0 and 3 are clearly positive. I also need to remember that this τ was built from the L13–15 o_proj writers, so L13 may not be fully independent here.\n\nNow I'm going after the mechanism behind L16 and L17, checking whether those heads attend to the guess and how their query and key changes line up. I also want to pin down what the L12 heads 0, 1, and 3 do in terms of their OV behavior, since their copy scores point in different directions.\n\nNow I'm ranking the components by how strongly they carry the effect: the L16 heads come first, with head 2 the largest in absolute terms, followed by L17 heads 0 and 1 as global copy heads, then the L17 MLP as the main writer into the logits. I'm also weighing the L12 query change and the L16 MLP as the next candidates.\n\nNext I'm checking the L17 down_proj's top singular direction: which units shift, whether that output lines up with τ, and how the gate and up projections change. I also want to see if L16's query or key changes point at the τ keys, and what the L12 rank-1 query heads 0, 1, and 3 write out through OV, possibly feeding later copy heads.\n\nI'm checking whether L12 heads write something that the L16/L17 keys read, which would mark the guess, so I'll run a composition test between the L12 head outputs and the L16/L17 key weights, including the change.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5668,"cache_read_input_tokens":205204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5668},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"ed6c40ec-be3b-40ab-b65f-24eaf0efe9d0","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:24:25.019Z","request_id":"req_011CgnTW8EvsoZaQ1j15Gmug","thinking_duration_ms":13615,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnTWBHjKRWu1K14dfPDC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 33 makes the central result robust to how τ is built. With a τ derived entirely without L16/L17 weights (L0–L2 readers vs L13–L15 writers; cos 0.77 with τ_att), all eight L16 and L17 heads show increased answer-token copying in A:\n- L16: +2.6, +3.7, +3.4, +3.1;\n- L17: +4.5, +2.8, +2.3, +1.9;\n- sum +24.2 vs a sign-flip null of −0.4 ± 4.8 (max of 40 draws 7.7), ≈ 5σ.\n\nL12–L15 are mixed with this τ (sum −2.8), except L15h0 (+3.4) and L15h3 (+4.8). This τ uses L13–L15 o_proj, so those layers are circular here. The finding I'm confident in: A's last two attention layers copy the answer token found in the prompt into the output more strongly than B's. The answer token present in the prompt is the user's guess, so A is the model trained to echo the guess. p(A) ≈ 0.85.\n\nNow the mechanism around these layers, for the component descriptions:\n1. Do the L16 and L17 query/key changes (the routing) target answer-token keys, as L17's did (key-direction T-fraction 0.19–0.24)? I'll measure the overlap of each head's top ΔW_Q-targeted key direction, and of ΔW_K's input directions, with τ against a random baseline.\n2. What does the L17 MLP change consist of? I'll look at the top singular component of ΔW_down: its unit loadings (which units), its output alignment with τ in logit space, and whether the same units' gate/up rows also changed (a coherent per-unit rewrite vs output-only).\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\nP=lambda L:f\"model.layers.{L}.\"\ndfin=1+A.get(\"model.norm.weight\")\ntau=np.load(\"/work/tau_indep.npy\"); tau_m=np.load(\"/work/tau_mlp.npy\")\nlt=A.config[\"layer_types\"]; hd=256\nrng=np.random.default_rng(1)\nfor L in [12,13,14,15,16,17]:\n    p=P(L); Di=1+A.get(p+\"input_layernorm.weight\")\n    theta=1e6 if lt[L]==\"full_attention\" else 1e4\n    f=theta**(-np.arange(128)/128.0); wp=np.cos(np.outer(f,np.arange(1,61))).mean(1); w=np.concatenate([wp,wp])\n    kn=1+A.get(p+\"self_attn.k_norm.weight\"); qn=1+A.get(p+\"self_attn.q_norm.weight\")\n    Wk=(A.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\")+B.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\"))/2\n    dq=A.get(p+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")\n    dk=A.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\")\n    out=[]\n    for h in range(4):\n        U,s,Vt=np.linalg.svd(dq[h*hd:(h+1)*hd],full_matrices=False)\n        kd=Di*(Wk.T@(kn*w*qn*U[:,0])); kd/=np.linalg.norm(kd)\n        out.append(abs(kd@tau))\n    Uk,sk,Vk=np.linalg.svd(dk,full_matrices=False)\n    kin=[abs((Vk[i]*Di)@tau)/np.linalg.norm(Vk[i]*Di) for i in range(3)]\n    print(f\"L{L} per-head dq->key-dir |cos tau|: {np.round(out,3)}   dWk input dirs |cos tau|: {np.round(kin,3)}  (random ~{1/np.sqrt(640):.3f})\")\n# L17 MLP down_proj top component\np=P(17); Dpf=1+A.get(p+\"post_feedforward_layernorm.weight\")\ndd=A.get(p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\")\nU,s,Vt=np.linalg.svd(dd,full_matrices=False)\nfor i in range(3):\n    o=dfin*Dpf*U[:,i]; o/=np.linalg.norm(o)\n    units=np.argsort(-np.abs(Vt[i]))[:10]\n    print(f\"L17 down sv{i} s={s[i]:.3f} energy={s[i]**2/np.sum(s**2):.3f} logit-dir |cos tau_indep|={abs(o@tau):.2f} |cos tau_mlp|={abs(o@tau_m):.2f}; top units {units} loadings {np.round(Vt[i][units],2)}; participation ratio {1/np.sum(Vt[i]**4):.0f}\")\ndg=A.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\"); du=A.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\")\nrown=np.sqrt((dg**2).sum(1)+(du**2).sum(1)); top=np.argsort(-np.abs(Vt[0]))[:10]\nprint(\"gate/up row-change of those units relative to median:\", np.round(rown[top]/np.median(rown),2))\nprint(\"corr over units of |Vt0| with input-row change:\", np.corrcoef(np.abs(Vt[0]),rown)[0,1].round(3))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5668,"cache_read_input_tokens":205204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5668},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"e7e2fd96-29ec-4dcf-9b16-04a4cf33ea0a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:24:38.582Z","request_id":"req_011CgnTW8EvsoZaQ1j15Gmug"}
